      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-14704",
      ":question/problem": "One end of a $34m$ wire is fixed to the ground at the point $A$, and the other end is tied to the top of a vertical pole. The foot of the pole is $30m$ from point $A$. To the nearest tenth of a degree, what is the measure of the angle formed by the wire and the ground? Assume that the ground between point $A$ and the foot of the pole is horizontal.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
