      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-5041",
      ":question/problem": "A soccer player aims to hit the top of a $3m$ tall goalpost for an exhibition show. The player is $15m$ from the goalpost. To the nearest tenth of a degree, at what angle to the horizontal must he hit the ball? Assume that the ball travels in a straight line and that the ground between the player and the goalpost is horizontal.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
